tinyquest is independently written from the published QUEST/Wahba mathematics:
the characteristic quartic's maximum root is solved by bounded Newton steps,
and the attitude is recovered using full adjugate columns.
It does not call the Davenport eigensolver or include source from AHRS,
SciPy, NumPy, or Vallado. Frozen numerical comparisons use independent
SciPy 1.18.1 Kabsch/SVD align_vectors results.
